WEBVTT

00:00:09.363 --> 00:00:10.823
[TRUNK DOOR CLOSES]

00:00:13.325 --> 00:00:14.660
[GASPS]

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:20.875
[GASPS]

00:00:24.963 --> 00:00:26.798
No!

00:00:34.179 --> 00:00:35.514
THOMAS: Peter.

00:00:35.514 --> 00:00:37.850
Where are the others?

00:00:40.561 --> 00:00:42.480
What have you done?

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:43.815
[SIGHS]

00:00:46.651 --> 00:00:48.402
THOMAS: Hey. I need all the addresses

00:00:48.402 --> 00:00:50.321
of the people who took those animals.

00:00:50.321 --> 00:00:53.324
We prefer "adopted those animals."

00:00:53.324 --> 00:00:57.036
And that information's private. Against the law to give it out.

00:00:58.121 --> 00:00:59.246
Mm...

00:01:00.498 --> 00:01:01.749
Go, Peter!

00:01:01.749 --> 00:01:03.960
[♪♪♪]

00:01:05.711 --> 00:01:08.422
Right. Here we go.

00:01:08.422 --> 00:01:10.967
"Almond milk, cashew cheese, walnut butter."

00:01:10.967 --> 00:01:13.011
This is not the list.

00:01:13.011 --> 00:01:16.597
The man clearly likes to get his protein from nuts.

00:01:16.597 --> 00:01:19.350
That is everything I have.

00:01:19.350 --> 00:01:20.392
[GRUNTS]

00:01:24.814 --> 00:01:27.942
"Manchester, London, Inverness, the Alps."

00:01:27.942 --> 00:01:30.528
They're everywhere. Do you see the mess you've made?

00:01:30.528 --> 00:01:33.280
You're never going to learn. You never give me a chance.

00:01:33.280 --> 00:01:35.700
All you do is tell me how bad I am.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:38.494
Well, then stop giving me reasons to.

00:01:38.494 --> 00:01:42.289
Wait, did you just talk? Uh, no. Yes. Maybe.

00:01:42.289 --> 00:01:44.834
Could be your imagination. Could be the radio.

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:48.838
[IMITATES RADIO DJ] This is BBC 7 playing all of the hits with none of the talk,

00:01:48.838 --> 00:01:50.798
especially not Peter. Rabbits can't talk.

00:01:50.798 --> 00:01:54.259
[IN REGULAR VOICE] Oh, look, the fuel gauge is empty.

00:01:54.259 --> 00:01:56.054
[ENGINE SPUTTERING, STOPS]

00:01:57.930 --> 00:01:59.306
[SIGHS]

00:02:00.141 --> 00:02:03.268
[CLICKS, WHISTLES]

00:02:03.268 --> 00:02:05.771
[IMITATES EXPLOSION] [THOMAS SCREAMS]

00:02:07.773 --> 00:02:09.775
PETER: I know I'm not perfect.

00:02:09.775 --> 00:02:11.694
But I can't do anything right by you.

00:02:11.694 --> 00:02:14.405
No matter what I do, you always assume the worst.

00:02:14.405 --> 00:02:17.992
Well, you got your entire family taken, Peter.

00:02:17.992 --> 00:02:19.952
If that's not the worst, what is?

00:02:19.952 --> 00:02:23.206
Why are you even helping me? I don't know.

00:02:23.206 --> 00:02:27.501
I just saw you and the others were in trouble and I came.

00:02:27.501 --> 00:02:29.128
[GRUNTING]

00:02:29.128 --> 00:02:31.630
It's not a choice.

00:02:31.630 --> 00:02:33.758
I don't think I'm actually propelling this

00:02:33.758 --> 00:02:35.467
in any real way.

00:02:35.467 --> 00:02:37.136
I'm sorry I wrecked your tomatoes.

00:02:37.136 --> 00:02:38.679
That wasn't supposed to happen.

00:02:38.679 --> 00:02:40.973
Then what was supposed to happen?

00:02:40.973 --> 00:02:43.308
[THOMAS PANTING, GROANING]

00:02:45.436 --> 00:02:46.854
I met someone who made me feel

00:02:46.854 --> 00:02:49.023
like not everything I did was wrong,

00:02:49.023 --> 00:02:51.358
who actually accepted me.

00:02:51.358 --> 00:02:53.027
But it was all a lie.

00:02:53.027 --> 00:02:55.113
He just used me. I'm so stupid.

00:02:56.447 --> 00:02:58.449
You're not stupid.

00:02:58.449 --> 00:03:00.576
You're young.

00:03:00.576 --> 00:03:02.203
So you make mistakes.

00:03:02.203 --> 00:03:03.537
A lot of mistakes.

00:03:03.537 --> 00:03:05.957
It's the one thing I'm really good at.

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:11.087
I know I'm too hard on you sometimes.

00:03:11.087 --> 00:03:14.048
I lost my father when I was very young too,

00:03:14.048 --> 00:03:17.093
so I never really learned how to be one.

00:03:17.093 --> 00:03:18.261
To me?

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:22.223
Yeah. To you.

00:03:22.223 --> 00:03:25.101
And to the others.

00:03:25.101 --> 00:03:27.270
That's why I'm here, I suppose.

00:03:27.270 --> 00:03:28.980
It's what a dad does.

00:03:28.980 --> 00:03:31.315
I didn't think I'd ever have a dad again.

00:03:31.315 --> 00:03:34.068
I didn't realize I already was one.

00:03:34.068 --> 00:03:36.403
[SIGHS]

00:03:36.403 --> 00:03:39.740
You're not the bad seed, Peter.

00:03:39.740 --> 00:03:41.826
I shouldn't have let them call you that.

00:03:41.826 --> 00:03:44.036
And I shouldn't have believed it.

00:03:44.036 --> 00:03:47.123
I know now that no one can tell me who I am.

00:03:48.666 --> 00:03:50.209
[CHUCKLES]

00:03:52.419 --> 00:03:56.632
I think there's someone we both love who needs to hear that too.

00:03:58.509 --> 00:04:01.595
About me talking, it's probably your imagination.

00:04:01.595 --> 00:04:02.972
[TRUCK CREAKING]

00:04:02.972 --> 00:04:04.431
You might also want to imagine

00:04:04.431 --> 00:04:06.684
your truck isn't rolling down the hill.

00:04:08.186 --> 00:04:09.728
No!

00:04:09.728 --> 00:04:13.191
Stop the truck! Please stop the truck! No! No!

00:04:13.191 --> 00:04:15.484
No! No!

00:04:15.484 --> 00:04:16.694
Oh, no!

00:04:16.694 --> 00:04:18.112
No! Ah! Ugh!

00:04:18.112 --> 00:04:20.656
No! No!

00:04:20.656 --> 00:04:24.160
[SOBBING] No, no.

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:25.410
No!

00:04:25.410 --> 00:04:27.288
NIGEL: So, what do you think, Bea?

00:04:27.288 --> 00:04:28.998
Pretty original.

00:04:28.998 --> 00:04:30.666
MAN: And that's just one idea

00:04:30.666 --> 00:04:33.252
the team came up with for a possible movie version.

00:04:33.252 --> 00:04:34.461
[EXECUTIVES MURMURING]

00:04:34.461 --> 00:04:36.881
Hm. They don't really look or act

00:04:36.881 --> 00:04:38.090
like my rabbits though.

00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:39.758
NIGEL: We couldn't be more excited.

00:04:39.758 --> 00:04:41.593
Your latest changes have brought us

00:04:41.593 --> 00:04:42.887
almost to the finish line.

00:04:42.887 --> 00:04:44.388
WOMAN 1: Yes, yes. WOMAN 2: So close.

00:04:44.388 --> 00:04:46.932
But I do think some of your pages are missing.

00:04:46.932 --> 00:04:48.893
The end is just the rabbits drinking tea

00:04:48.893 --> 00:04:51.478
and apologizing to each other. Oh, no, that's right.

00:04:51.478 --> 00:04:54.357
They learn from their mistakes. EXECUTIVES: Ugh.

00:04:54.357 --> 00:04:56.775
NIGEL: What we're trying to say is, the ending

00:04:56.775 --> 00:04:58.319
is really important.

00:04:58.319 --> 00:05:00.279
It's the only thing readers remember.

00:05:00.279 --> 00:05:03.490
EXECUTIVES: Yes. Okay, uh, well, um, what about

00:05:03.490 --> 00:05:05.368
if one of them goes into the village

00:05:05.368 --> 00:05:07.745
to get a birthday present?

00:05:07.745 --> 00:05:09.288
[ALL GROAN]

00:05:09.288 --> 00:05:11.207
And gets kidnapped. EXECUTIVES: Yes!

00:05:11.207 --> 00:05:14.543
They should all get kidnapped. There can be a rescue mission,

00:05:14.543 --> 00:05:16.628
exotic locations all over the country,

00:05:16.628 --> 00:05:18.339
even outside the country.

00:05:18.339 --> 00:05:21.342
And you can have chases on many different types of vehicles,

00:05:21.342 --> 00:05:24.387
like race cars. Boats, motorcycles, planes.

00:05:24.387 --> 00:05:27.181
That they can jump out of. Then they can team together

00:05:27.181 --> 00:05:29.058
to get revenge on a gang of bad guys.

00:05:29.058 --> 00:05:31.310
And then they ride off into the sunset.

00:05:31.310 --> 00:05:33.229
But the sky should be pink.

00:05:33.229 --> 00:05:36.107
Because that's the color of hope and the future.

00:05:36.107 --> 00:05:37.566
EXECUTIVES: Aw...

00:05:37.566 --> 00:05:40.903
Now, if the ending is as action-packed

00:05:40.903 --> 00:05:42.529
as we all agreed it should be...

00:05:42.529 --> 00:05:43.989
I don't know if we all agreed.

00:05:43.989 --> 00:05:45.116
[EXECUTIVES LAUGHING]

00:05:45.116 --> 00:05:48.535
Bea! I'm so sorry to interrupt.

00:05:48.535 --> 00:05:49.870
NIGEL: Thomas!

00:05:49.870 --> 00:05:51.872
So good to see you. Nigel.

00:05:51.872 --> 00:05:55.209
Ah, and you brought Peter. Terrific.

00:05:55.209 --> 00:05:56.961
Now we can show everyone

00:05:56.961 --> 00:05:59.671
what Peter would look like in zero gravity.

00:05:59.671 --> 00:06:01.966
[IMITATES FILTERED BREATHING]

00:06:01.966 --> 00:06:05.261
Mopsy! Cotton-Tail! Let's get back to the rocket ship.

00:06:05.261 --> 00:06:07.679
[EXECUTIVES LAUGHING]

00:06:07.679 --> 00:06:09.848
Nigel, stop it! What?

00:06:09.848 --> 00:06:11.434
BEA: Goodness me. Ooh!

00:06:11.434 --> 00:06:13.936
Come here. Are you okay, sweetie?

00:06:13.936 --> 00:06:16.147
The other rabbits were taken. What?

00:06:16.147 --> 00:06:18.565
And the pig and the duck and the hedgehog,

00:06:18.565 --> 00:06:20.025
and is there a badger?

00:06:20.025 --> 00:06:23.362
Yeah, I need your car to go and get them.

00:06:23.362 --> 00:06:25.656
My goodness. Oh...

00:06:25.656 --> 00:06:28.159
How did this happen? What have I done?

00:06:28.159 --> 00:06:30.953
You've written 80 percent of a best seller.

00:06:30.953 --> 00:06:33.872
Just get some more rabbits. You can get a million more

00:06:33.872 --> 00:06:35.916
with the money you're about to make.

00:06:35.916 --> 00:06:37.918
Huh? No. I-- I'm very sorry,

00:06:37.918 --> 00:06:39.544
but I can't do this.

00:06:39.544 --> 00:06:42.423
This isn't my world. Not your world? Heh.

00:06:42.423 --> 00:06:43.966
Look around you.

00:06:43.966 --> 00:06:47.094
You created all this.

00:06:47.094 --> 00:06:49.305
This is your world.

00:06:49.305 --> 00:06:52.391
There's no boat chases or skiing in my world.

00:06:52.391 --> 00:06:55.144
And there's certainly no rabbits jumping out of planes.

00:06:55.144 --> 00:06:56.520
Bea.

